            %p
              Here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
              denotes any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement"} cofibrant replacement
              (which exists, by
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "functorial+factorization#InCombinatorialModelCategories"} this Example
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C',A]
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
              by the above discussion) and the double arrow denotes (the image under the hc-nerve of) the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              with components the corresponding resolution equivalences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∼
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mtext -
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\text{-}) \xrightarrow{\;\sim\;} (\text{-})
              (which are components of a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functorial+factorization"} functorial factorization
            %p
              The left square commutes by the construction of right derived functors of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+functors"} right Quillen functors
              (eg.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "Introduction+to+Homotopy+Theory#ComputationOfLeftRightDerivedFunctorsViaResolutions"} this Prop.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/naturality+square"} naturality square
              of the comparison map discussed
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#ModelCategoryPresentation"} above
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibrant+objects"} bifibrant objects
            %p
              The total diagram is of the claimed from. It just remains to see that the 2-morphism filling it is really an equivalence, but this follows by Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalencesDetectedOnObjects"}
          %p
            %br/
          %h3#Limits Limits and colimits
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            an ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            that admits small
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Func
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(D,C)
            has all small limits and colimits, and these are computed objectwise. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits+and+colimits+by+example"} limits and colimits by example
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "-functors" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              has all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+in+a+quasi-category"} colimits
              indexed by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              be a small quasi-category. Then
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Func
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(D,C)
                  has all
                  = succeed "-indexed" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %li
                %p
                  A morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi K
                          %mo ▹
                        %mo →
                        %mi Func
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi D
                        %mo ,
                        %mi C
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\triangleright \to Func(D,C)
                  is a colimiting cocone precisely if for each object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in D
                  the induced morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi K
                          %mo ▹
                        %mo →
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^\triangleright \to C
                  is a colimiting cocone.
            %p
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#Lurie"}> Lurie, corollary 5.1.2.3
            ).
          %h3#equivalences Equivalences
          %p
          #EquivalencesDetectedOnObjects.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (equivalences of
                = succeed "-functors" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %br/
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(D,C)
              (that is, a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} equivalence
              if and only if each component
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_d
              is an equivalence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %br/
          %p
            This is due to
            %a{:href => "#Joyal08"} Joyal (2008), Chapter 5, Theorem C (
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/JoyalTheoryOfQuasiCategories.pdf#page=125"} p. 125
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Between ordinary categories, it reproduces the ordinary
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+functors"} category of functors
            %li
              %p
                Since the standard
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
                presents
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo ≃
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (sSet_{Quillen})^\circ \simeq \infty Grpd
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
                (more precisely and more generally the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+sSet-enriched+presheaves"} model structure on sSet-enriched presheaves
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} opposite (∞,1)-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presents
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-presheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-presheaves
                on
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi sSet
                        %mi Quillen
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Func
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi PSh
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      N([C^{op},sSet_{Quillen}]^\circ) \simeq Func(C^{op},\infty Grpd)
                      \= PSh_{(\infty,1)}(C)
                      \\,.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor+2-category"} 2-functor 2-category
          %h2#references References
          %p The intrinsic definition is in section 1.2.7 of
          %ul
            %li#Lurie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
